. Those are concerns. For C, we have strengths: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology; concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also we have note \"excellent attention skills\" for C. So we need to decide whether to stick with B or shift to C. The panel currently leaning C. As Sofia, we can reconsider. We should evaluate if any new evidence changes our view. We have not yet discussed Candidate A and D. But we can still keep B if we think B is better. However we need to be evidence-based. Let's compare B vs C: B: high stress resilience, conscientiousness, technical (weather, computer). C: reliability, crew atmosphere, decision quality, calmness, technical understanding. Both have communication concerns. B's communication issues include pretentious, wrong tone, nasty remarks. C's communication difficulty and egocentric. Which is more severe? Nasty remarks about colleagues may be more severe for crew cooperation. C's difficulty communicating ideas may affect safety but less severe? Also C's reliability is 100% vs B's conscientiousness (good but not proven reliability). Decision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly. B no explicit decision quality. Stress resilience: B handles stress well; C keeps calm in crisis (similar). Technical competence: B good at weather, computer; C understands complicated technology. Both good.\n\nThus C seems stronger overall. As Sofia, we can update our recommendation to C, acknowledging the stronger reliability and decision quality. Provide evidence. Also note that B's communication issues (nasty remarks) are more concerning. So we shift vote to C.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: agree with Anna and Markus that C is strong, but also note we originally favored B due to stress resilience, but after hearing about C's reliability and decision quality, we change.\n\nThus public message: I change my vote to C, explain why.\n\nMetadata JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
